From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Joonhoe Kim <26rote@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 00:31:55 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] Bluetooth: qca: check the device address on every setup

qca_check_bdaddr() sets HCI_QUIRK_USE_BDADDR_PROPERTY when the controller
reports the default address from its NVM file. The controller then starts
unconfigured unless devicetree provides an address, and
hci_dev_setup_sync() programs the configured address again on every
later setup, which controllers with HCI_QUIRK_NON_PERSISTENT_SETUP need.
The check is skipped once hdev->public_addr has been set.

That leaves the quirk unset when the first setup does not reach the
check. If the rampatch or NVM file cannot be loaded, for instance because
the driver is built in and the firmware is not in the initramfs, setup
continues with the ROM firmware (QCA_ROM_FW) and the controller comes up
configured. When user space then sets the address with
MGMT_OP_SET_PUBLIC_ADDRESS, the next setup loads the NVM file and the
address is programmed once because HCI_CONFIG is set. Every later power
on runs setup again without the quirk, so the controller falls back to
the default address from the NVM file and devices bonded to the
configured address no longer connect. Seen with a WCN7850-type controller
on a Lenovo Legion Tab Gen 5 (TB323FU) after powering the adapter off and
on.

Read the address back on every setup, so that the quirk is set whenever
the controller uses the default address. This costs one Read BD_ADDR
command per setup. Setting the quirk while hdev->public_addr is set does
not make the controller unconfigured, as is_configured() only considers
it while no address has been set.

Controllers with a valid address of their own still lose an address set
by user space on the next setup; that is not changed here.

Fixes: 32868e126c78 ("Bluetooth: qca: fix invalid device address check")
Cc: stable@vger.kernel.org	# 6.5
Signed-off-by: Joonhoe Kim <26rote@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/bluetooth/btqca.c | 3 ---
 1 file changed, 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/bluetooth/btqca.c b/drivers/bluetooth/btqca.c
index 64ecf052e..f15340fa8 100644
--- a/drivers/bluetooth/btqca.c
+++ b/drivers/bluetooth/btqca.c
@@ -696,9 +696,6 @@ static int qca_check_bdaddr(struct hci_dev *hdev, const struct qca_fw_config *co
 	struct sk_buff *skb;
 	int err;
 
-	if (bacmp(&hdev->public_addr, BDADDR_ANY))
-		return 0;
-
 	skb = __hci_cmd_sync(hdev, HCI_OP_READ_BD_ADDR, 0, NULL,
 			     HCI_INIT_TIMEOUT);
 	if (IS_ERR(skb)) {
-- 
2.47.3

